               WITNESS IDENTIFICATION AND QUALIFICATIONS

Q.   Please state your name and business address.

A.   My name is Yen H. Ly. My business address is 401 Nicollet Mall, Minneapolis, Minnesota

     55401.

Q.   On whose behalf are you testifying in this proceeding?

A.   I am filing testimony on behalf of Southwestern Public Service Company, a New Mexico

     corporation (“SPS”) and wholly-owned electric utility subsidiary of Xcel Energy Inc.

     (“Xcel Energy”).

Q.   Have you previously filed testimony in this proceeding?

A.   No. My colleague, Tamra Newman, submitted Direct Testimony in this proceeding in

     support of SPS’s request to recover in rates the cost of our employee compensation and

     benefits, which are elements of Xcel Energy’s Total Rewards Program. I am taking Ms.

     Newman’s place as SPS’s witness for these topics for the remainder of the proceeding. I

     adopt Ms. Newman’s Direct Testimony as if it were my own.

Q.   By whom are you employed and in what position?

A.   I am employed by Xcel Energy Services, Inc. (“XES”) as Vice President, Total Rewards.

     XES is a wholly owned subsidiary of Xcel Energy Inc. (“Xcel Energy”) and provides an

     array of support to SPS and the other utility operating company subsidiaries of Xcel Energy

     on a coordinated basis.

Q.   Please outline your responsibilities as Vice President, Total Rewards.

A.   As the Vice President, Total Rewards, I oversee Xcel Energy’s total rewards programs and

     I am responsible for establishing the strategic direction to competitively position Xcel

     Energy’s compensation and benefits offerings to attract and retain employees.


                                              1
                                         EXHIBIT A


Q.   Please describe your educational background.

A.   I received a Bachelor of Arts degree in Marketing and a Master of Business Administration

     from the University of Minnesota. I also have the Certified Compensation Professional and

     the Certified Global Renumeration Professional designations from WorldatWork.

Q.   Please describe your professional experience.

A.   Prior to joining Xcel Energy Services, I worked in various industries and served in different

     total rewards leadership capacities for domestic and global companies. The following are

     several organizations I previously worked for: Patterson Companies, Donaldson,

     Medtronic, and Graco.




